The implementation translates cleanly and passes CPython checks for empty, ASCII, and Unicode input. I’m now encoding the relevant Python evaluation rules (module loading, function binding, conditionals, attributes, and calls) plus MD5 itself over UTF‑8 bytes, including padding and all 64 rounds; this keeps concrete `krun` results independent of CPython’s `hashlib`.
